// Bandit Level 21 → Level 22

URL: https://overthewire.org/wargames/bandit/

Step1: Log in to the Bandit Level 21 server:

        ssh bandit21@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step2: Enter the password obtained from Bandit Level 20.

Step3: The challenge tells us that a program is running automatically using `cron`.

Step4: Go to the cron configuration directory:

        cd /etc/cron.d

Step5: List the files:

        ls

Step6: We can see a file related to the next level:

        cronjob_bandit22

Step7: Read the cron job:

        cat cronjob_bandit22

Step8: We see something like:

        * * * * * bandit22 /usr/bin/cronjob_bandit22.sh &> /dev/null

Step9: This means the script `/usr/bin/cronjob_bandit22.sh` is executed every minute as the `bandit22` user.

Step10: Read the script:

        cat /usr/bin/cronjob_bandit22.sh

Step11: The script contains:

        #!/bin/bash
        chmod 644 /tmp/t7O6lds9S0RqQh9aMcz6ShpAoZKF7fgv
        cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit22 > /tmp/t7O6lds9S0RqQh9aMcz6ShpAoZKF7fgv

Step12: The important part is:

        cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit22 > /tmp/t7O6lds9S0RqQh9aMcz6ShpAoZKF7fgv

Step13: The cron job copies the Bandit Level 22 password into a file in `/tmp`.

Step14: It also runs:

        chmod 644 /tmp/t7O6lds9S0RqQh9aMcz6ShpAoZKF7fgv

Step15: Permission `644` means that everyone can read the file.

Step16: Read the file:

        cat /tmp/t7O6lds9S0RqQh9aMcz6ShpAoZKF7fgv

Step17: The password for Bandit Level 22 is:

        tRae0UfB9v0UzbCdn9cY0gQnds9GF58Q

Step18: The Bandit Level 21 → Level 22 challenge is solved.

